# Everything the image does not need. Two reasons this matters beyond build speed:
#   1. Smaller context = faster, more cache-friendly builds.
#   2. Anything sent to the daemon can end up in an image layer by accident.
#      Excluding credentials here is a second line of defence behind gitleaks.

# ── VCS & CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# ── Infrastructure: none of it is part of the application image ─────────────
k8s/
infra/
argocd/
observability/
ansible/
docker/

# ── Docs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
*.html
LICENSE
docs/

# ── Tooling config: used by CI and by humans, never by the image ───────────
# Verified with a probe build (`COPY . /ctx` + `find`) rather than assumed —
# these had been slipping into the context because they were added to the repo
# after this file was first written. repo-guide.html alone was 94 KB of context
# transferred on every build for nothing.
scripts/
trivy.yaml
.yamllint.yml
.dockerignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig

# ── Secrets & local state: must never reach the build context ──────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*-key.json
*credentials*.json
kubeconfig
.kube/
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.trivyignore

# ── Go build artefacts & tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files are excluded deliberately: they are a CI gate (Task 7), not a
# runtime artefact, and shipping them would only widen the image.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
bin/
dist/
vendor/
coverage.out
*.test

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
